00:37:28,888 --> 00:37:34,888
The Cove is a 2009 American documentary film directed by Louie Psihoyos that
analyzes and questions dolphin hunting practices in Japan.

12
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:59,333
It was awarded the Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature in 2010.

13
00:44:17,777 --> 00:44:23,777
The film is a call to action to halt mass dolphin kills and captures, change Japanese fishing practices, and inform and
educate the public about captivity and the increasing hazard of mercury poisoning from consuming dolphin meat.

14
00:47:42,222 --> 00:47:48,222
Psihoyos is a former-National Geographic photographer and a co-founder of the Oceanic Preservation
Society, and the film is presented from an ocean conservationist's point of view.

15
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Portions were filmed secretly in 2007 using underwater microphones
and high-definition cameras disguised as rocks.

16
00:54:31,111 --> 00:54:37,111
The film highlights the fact that the number of dolphins killed in the Taiji dolphin drive hunt is several times greater than the number of whales
killed in the Antarctic, and asserts that 23,000 dolphins and porpoises are killed in Japan every year by the country's whaling industry.

17
00:57:55,555 --> 00:58:01,555
The migrating dolphins are herded into a cove where they are netted off.

18
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
The young and pretty are sold to oceanariums and dolphinariums
around the world, and the rest are brutally slaughtered.

19
01:04:44,444 --> 01:04:50,444
The film argues that dolphin hunting as practiced
in Japan is unnecessary and cruel.

20
01:08:08,888 --> 01:08:14,888
Since the film's release, The Cove has drawn controversy over its supposed lack of
neutrality, secret filming techniques,  and accusations of anti-Japanese sentiment.

21
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:39,333
Nevertheless, the film received predominantly positive reviews from critics.

22
01:14:57,777 --> 01:15:03,777
It won the U.S.

23
01:18:22,222 --> 01:18:28,222
Audience Award at the 25th annual Sundance Film Festival in January 2009.

24
01:21:46,666 --> 01:21:52,666
It was selected out of 879 submissions in the category.

25
01:25:11,111 --> 01:25:17,111
The film explores themes of dying and death, japan, suffering, ocean, dolphin.

26
01:28:35,555 --> 01:28:41,555
The tone is dark.
